[line]
[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install with a mod manager and the dependencies come with it. To install manually, drop the DLL into [font=Courier New]BepInEx/plugins[/font] and install each dependency below.
[list]
[*][url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/denikson/BepInExPack_Valheim/]BepInExPack Valheim 5.4.2333[/url] — mod loader.
[*][url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/ValheimModding/JsonDotNET/]JsonDotNET 13.0.4[/url] — persists compile sessions to disk.
[*][url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/ValheimModding/Jotunn/]Jotunn 2.29.0[/url] — server-authoritative config sync.
[*][url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/ZenDragon/ZenMap/]ZenMap ≥ 1.8.0[/url] — required for MAP COMPILE; also fixes a [font=Courier New]Graphics.CopyTexture[/font] size-mismatch on expanded worlds.
[/list]
[quote]ZenMap already depends on Jotunn, so most setups have Jotunn already. Install on every client that wants the buttons; install on the server too to push synced settings.[/quote]
[line]
[size=4][b]Quick start[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Open the large map ([font=Courier New]M[/font], or interact with a cartography table).
[*][b]Share one view:[/b] click [b]COPY MAP[/b] ([font=Courier New]F11[/font]) and paste into Discord, or set a webhook and click [b]SEND MAP[/b] ([font=Courier New]F10[/font]).
[*][b]Build a stitched map:[/b] click [b]START COMPILE[/b], then [b]ADD TILE[/b] at each cartography table you visit. When you've covered the ground you want, click [b]COMPILE[/b] → [b]SAVE[/b] / [b]COPY[/b] / [b]SEND TO DISCORD[/b].
[/list]
[line]
